{
  "name": "RAN · Post-Ingestion",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "ran/post-ingest",
        "responseMode": "lastNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "webhook-post-ingest",
      "name": "Webhook post-ingest",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [240, 300],
      "webhookId": "ran-post-ingest"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "v1",
              "name": "vendor",
              "value": "={{ $json.body?.vendor ?? $json.vendor ?? 'nokia' }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "v2",
              "name": "snapshot_date",
              "value": "={{ $json.body?.snapshot_date ?? $json.snapshot_date ?? '' }}",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "v3",
              "name": "snapshot_dates",
              "value": "={{ ($json.body?.snapshot_date ?? $json.snapshot_date) ? [($json.body?.snapshot_date ?? $json.snapshot_date)] : [] }}",
              "type": "array"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "normalize",
      "name": "Normaliser payload",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [500, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $env.RAN_BACKEND_URL || 'http://host.docker.internal:8010' }}/guardian/run",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Authorization",
              "value": "=Bearer {{ $env.RAN_API_TOKEN }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "Content-Type",
              "value": "application/json"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ snapshot_dates: $json.snapshot_dates }) }}",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "neverError": true
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "guardian-run",
      "name": "Guardian run",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [760, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $env.RAN_BACKEND_URL || 'http://host.docker.internal:8010' }}/integrations/powerbi/sync",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "Authorization",
              "value": "=Bearer {{ $env.RAN_API_TOKEN }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "neverError": true
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "powerbi-sync",
      "name": "Power BI sync",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [1020, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## RAN · Post-Ingestion\n\n**Webhook** : `POST /webhook/ran/post-ingest`\n\n**Variables n8n** (Settings → Variables ou `.env.identity`) :\n- `RAN_API_TOKEN` — JWT admin **après reset DB**\n- `RAN_BACKEND_URL` — `http://host.docker.internal:8010`\n\n**Corps attendu** (optionnel) :\n```json\n{ \"vendor\": \"nokia\", \"snapshot_date\": \"2026-06-26\" }\n```\n\n⚠️ Ne pas utiliser `localhost:8010` dans les nœuds HTTP — n8n tourne dans Docker.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 400
      },
      "id": "note",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [200, 40]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Webhook post-ingest": {
      "main": [[{ "node": "Normaliser payload", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]]
    },
    "Normaliser payload": {
      "main": [[{ "node": "Guardian run", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]]
    },
    "Guardian run": {
      "main": [[{ "node": "Power BI sync", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]]
    }
  },
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1"
  },
  "active": false
}
